@* Short, cited excerpts from published relationship research and couples therapists, shown on
   the home page. Every quote here was checked word for word against the linked source on
   2026-11-10. Rules for editing this list:
   - Quote only what the linked page actually says, and keep each excerpt short (fair use).
   - Attribute to the person or organisation the source names; say "quoted in" for secondhand.
   - Never imply the source endorses or is affiliated with BridgeTogether. *@

<section class="expert-perspectives" aria-labelledby="expert-perspectives-heading">
    <h2 id="expert-perspectives-heading">What relationship researchers and therapists say</h2>
    <p class="expert-perspectives-intro">
        BridgeTogether's features are shaped by ideas that are widely shared in published couples research.
        Here are a few, in the experts' own words.
    </p>

    <ul class="expert-perspectives-list">
        @foreach (var item in Items)
        {
            <li>
                <figure class="expert-quote">
                    <blockquote cite="@item.Url">
                        <p>&ldquo;@item.Quote&rdquo;</p>
                    </blockquote>
                    <figcaption>
                        <span class="expert-quote-who">@item.Who</span>
                        <cite>
                            <a href="@item.Url" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@item.Source<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
                        </cite>
                    </figcaption>
                    <p class="expert-quote-link">@item.HowWeUseIt</p>
                </figure>
            </li>
        }
    </ul>

    <p class="expert-perspectives-note">
        Short excerpts are quoted for commentary; follow each link to read the full piece.
        The people and organisations quoted are not affiliated with BridgeTogether and have not
        reviewed or endorsed it.
    </p>
</section>

